    "CARD SPLIT (teacher's divisions): 0:00:13 bab intro/khidma-sukna mu'aqqat & mu'abbad (→0:02:47); 0:02:49 «فإن خرجت رقبة العبد» thulth, muhaya, dar in thirds, no sale (→0:06:41); 0:06:42 musa lahu dies + 0:07:53 ghalla but used himself (→0:10:11, merged: both short, same 'what he gets' theme); 0:10:14 no ijara, Shafi'i (→0:14:19); 0:14:32 Kufa + 0:15:26 ghalla again/qisma (→0:17:29); 0:17:46 raqaba & khidma + nazair + fasl (→0:24:21); 0:24:27 thamara/ghalla + 0:26:40 suf/awlad/laban (→0:30:54); 0:30:57 bab wasiyyat al-dhimmi: bi'a built, named, unnamed, farq (→0:36:31); 0:36:33 four kinds + sahib al-hawa (→0:40:18); 0:40:22 musta'min + 0:42:53 dhimmi (→0:43:52).",
    "TEACHER SLIPS (cards follow the book): (a) 0:31:57 for the first dhimmi masala (bi'a built in health) he says «وہ وقف، وہ وصیت، وہ باطل ہو جائے گا» — no wasiya there; book: Sahibayn «فلأن هذه معصية: فلا تصح» (the building as waqf is invalid) and it is «ميراث» by agreement; card says 'not a waqf, inherited'. (b) 0:37:10–0:37:16 khinzir example: «یہ درست نہیں ہے۔ امام ابو حنیفہ کے ہاں درست ہے …» — self-corrected; book puts it «على الخلاف إذا كان لقوم غير مسمين» (teacher omits the 'unnamed' qualifier; footnote: for named people valid by ijma'); card adds the qualifier from book. (c) 0:38:02–0:38:12 second kind for named people: «اس خاتون کا یہ کہنا» (= اس آدمی) and «باقی ورثاء کی مرضی ہے» — it is the named recipients' choice (footnote: «إن شاءوا فعلوا ذلك، وإن شاءوا تركوا»), as he himself said at 0:38:02 «ان کی مرضی»; card says ان کی مرضی. (d) 0:23:11–0:23:54 the raqaba-then-khidma case is put as «امام محمد کے ہاں»; in the book it is part of Muhammad's reasoning but the ruling is agreed (Abu Yusuf's own proof cites it: «كما في وصية الرقبة والخدمة»; footnote: mawsul and mafsul equal there); card gives the ruling without restricting it to Muhammad. (e) 0:30:31 «باندی کا بچہ» in the suf/awlad summary — the book's case is the flock (غنم); not carded. (f) 0:42:48 «ظاہر روایت یہ ہے کہ … وصیت ہو سکتی ہے»: the matn does not use the words ظاهر الرواية, it states «جاز» then «وعن أبي حنيفة وأبي يوسف: أنه لا يجوز»; card labels 'ظاہر روایت' as the teacher's. (g) 0:09:41 debt example «گھر بھی واپس دے دو» — the book's point is only that the ghalla can be taken back («بالاسترداد منه بعد استغلالها»), the house is not his; card omits 'house back'. (h) 0:17:55 vs 0:18:41: the khidma recipient is «بکر» then «خالد» (raqaba = Zayd both times); card uses بکر in tamheed and the book's terms after. (i) 0:18:50–0:18:55 'after the term / after the khidma recipient's death the slave goes to Zayd' is the teacher's inference from card 3, not stated on 1342; card labels it «استاد کی وضاحت». (j) 0:00:13 he reads the heading with «والصوف» (not in this print).",
